{"title":"FreshMart","sub":"A hard discounter is coming. How should a regional grocer respond?","type":"Competitive response","industry":"Grocery retail","geo":"United States (Midwest)","diff":2,"fmt":"Candidate-led","time":"30 min","skills":"Sizing the threat · comparing responses to doing nothing","prompt":"FreshMart operates 60 supermarkets in the US Midwest. A European hard discounter (small stores, ~1,500 products, prices 20-30% below supermarkets) has announced 25 new stores in FreshMart's region over the next three years. FreshMart's CEO wants a plan to respond.","clarify":[{"q":"FreshMart economics?","a":"Average store sells $20M a year; EBIT margin 4%. Contribution on each lost dollar of sales ≈ 25%."},{"q":"Overlap?","a":"30 of FreshMart's 60 stores are within 3 miles of a planned discounter store."},{"q":"What happens elsewhere?","a":"In other regions, supermarkets near a new discounter lost ~12% of sales in year 1 and ~8% for good."},{"q":"Strengths?","a":"Strong fresh food, local brand, good service; prices ~10% above market average."}],"structure":{"root":"How should FreshMart respond?","branches":[{"head":"Size the threat","items":["Stores exposed","Sales and profit at risk","Which customers / categories"]},{"head":"Options","items":["Do nothing","Match prices on key items","Private label","Differentiate: fresh, service, loyalty"]},{"head":"Choose","items":["Impact vs cost","Speed","Risk of price war"]}]},"hypothesis":"The threat is concentrated in half the stores, so a targeted response probably beats a chain-wide price cut.","questions":[{"q":"How much profit is at risk if FreshMart does nothing?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Sales lost for good = 30 stores × $20M × 8% = <b>$48M/year</b>. Profit lost = $48M × 25% = <b>$12M/year</b>.</p> <p>Total EBIT = 60 × $20M × 4% = $48M → doing nothing costs <b>a quarter of FreshMart's profit</b>.</p>"},{"q":"Which customers leave? Look at this exhibit.","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://